//! The execution core: load a precompiled module once, then drive snippets with
//! the deterministic-replay tool loopback.
//!
//! quickjs runs SYNCHRONOUSLY on the vendored interpreter. When the guest makes
//! a host call (`ferrite.callTool`, `env.store(...).get`, `fetch`, ...) it writes
//! a request frame and blocks on stdin; the shim aborts the read (a `TOOL_PENDING`
//! trap) so control returns to async Rust. The host services the call, appends
//! the response, and re-runs the (deterministic) program from the top with all
//! prior responses preloaded. Each distinct call index therefore executes its
//! side effect exactly once, and an unbounded async host call is serviced
//! between two fully-synchronous wasm runs — no threads, no reentrancy.

